{"type":"assistant","uuid":"1303da2a-e77b-455f-97f1-8411faa555da","session_id":"4163bdfc-3a81-4fb8-be42-5517abb2c26a","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"1303da2a-e77b-455f-97f1-8411faa555da","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The bug is about the \"confirm password\" field not showing the password when the visibility toggle is tapped. The key finding is:\n\n1. The primary password field uses `TextInputLayout` with `app:passwordToggleEnabled=\"true\"` - this gives it a built-in visibility toggle icon.\n2. The confirm password field is a plain `EditText` without a `TextInputLayout` wrapper - it has NO visibility toggle icon at all.\n\nSo the bug is that when the user taps the visibility icon on the primary password field, the confirm field doesn't update to show/hide in sync.\n\nThe fix should be:\n- For the initial setup flow (IntroScreenActivity), the confirm field should show/hide when the primary password visibility toggle is tapped.\n- This needs a TextWatcher or some listener that syncs the visibility state of both fields.\n\nLet me look at the specific Java source files to understand how to fix this. The bug happens \"when setting password/PIN the first time\" which points to `IntroScreenActivity.java`. Let me read the relevant files to understand the exact fix needed.\n\nLooking at the analysis:\n- The confirm password field has NO visibility toggle of its own - it's a plain `EditText`\n- The primary password field has the Material Design `passwordToggleEnabled` feature\n- When the user taps the eye icon on the primary field, it shows/hides that field's content\n- But the confirm field doesn't mirror this visibility state\n\nThe fix should sync the password visibility between the two fields. When the primary password field's visibility changes, the confirm field's visibility should change too.\n\nLet me read the source files to understand the implementation.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"7c6102d4-bb43-4cbd-9dfb-2889721f0e9d","session_id":"4163bdfc-3a81-4fb8-be42-5517abb2c26a","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"7c6102d4-bb43-4cbd-9dfb-2889721f0e9d","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nNow I understand the bug. The primary password field has a visibility toggle (via `TextInputLayout.passwordToggleEnabled`), but the confirm password field is a plain `EditText` with no toggle and doesn't sync its visibility state when the primary field's toggle is pressed.\n\nLet me read the source files that handle initial password setup to implement the fix.\n\n\n\n\n"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
