{"type":"assistant","uuid":"375d7726-273d-43f5-bbb0-d37dede22530","session_id":"4163bdfc-3a81-4fb8-be42-5517abb2c26a","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"375d7726-273d-43f5-bbb0-d37dede22530","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me provide a final summary of the fix.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"278fb603-a516-4d85-bfa6-2a98a6510969","session_id":"4163bdfc-3a81-4fb8-be42-5517abb2c26a","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"278fb603-a516-4d85-bfa6-2a98a6510969","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe patch is written to `password-visibility-sync.patch`. Here's a summary of the fix:\n\n## Bug Summary\n\n**Issue:** When the user taps the visibility icon (\"eye\" button) to show the password/PIN in the primary field, the confirm password field remains masked because it has no visibility toggle and doesn't sync its display state with the primary field.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe Material Design `TextInputLayout` with `app:passwordToggleEnabled=\"true\"` provides a visibility toggle via an internal `CompoundButton` (stored as `mPasswordToggleView`). When toggled, it changes the text filter on the primary field. However, the confirm field is a plain `EditText` with `PasswordTransformationMethod` applied — it has no toggle and no connection to the primary field's visibility state.\n\n## Fix\n\nFor each of the 4 locations where password+confirm fields appear:\n\n1. **IntroScreenActivity.java** — First-time app setup wizard\n2. **CredentialsPreference.java** — Settings: auth method selection  \n3. **PasswordEncryptedPreference.java** — Settings: backup password/PIN\n4. **PasswordEntryDialog.java** — Backup restore dialog\n\nAdded a reflection-based hook into Material Design's internal password toggle (`TextInputLayout.mPasswordToggleView`). When the toggle's checked state changes, the confirm field's transformation method is synced:\n- **Checked (show):** `passwordConfirm.setTransformationMethod(null)` — displays text unmasked\n- **Unchecked (hide):** `passwordConfirm.setTransformationMethod(new PasswordTransformationMethod())` — displays text masked\n\nThe reflection is wrapped in try/catch to gracefully handle cases where the internal API might change or be unavailable."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":89589,"output_tokens":360,"cache_read_input_tokens":85936,"total_tokens":89949}}}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","uuid":"a1810ef4-f6ce-4513-bc00-200dd6c40a1c","session_id":"4163bdfc-3a81-4fb8-be42-5517abb2c26a","is_error":false,"duration_ms":333979,"duration_api_ms":255898,"num_turns":3,"result":"\n\nThe patch is written to `password-visibility-sync.patch`. Here's a summary of the fix:\n\n## Bug Summary\n\n**Issue:** When the user taps the visibility icon (\"eye\" button) to show the password/PIN in the primary field, the confirm password field remains masked because it has no visibility toggle and doesn't sync its display state with the primary field.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe Material Design `TextInputLayout` with `app:passwordToggleEnabled=\"true\"` provides a visibility toggle via an internal `CompoundButton` (stored as `mPasswordToggleView`). When toggled, it changes the text filter on the primary field. However, the confirm field is a plain `EditText` with `PasswordTransformationMethod` applied — it has no toggle and no connection to the primary field's visibility state.\n\n## Fix\n\nFor each of the 4 locations where password+confirm fields appear:\n\n1. **IntroScreenActivity.java** — First-time app setup wizard\n2. **CredentialsPreference.java** — Settings: auth method selection  \n3. **PasswordEncryptedPreference.java** — Settings: backup password/PIN\n4. **PasswordEntryDialog.java** — Backup restore dialog\n\nAdded a reflection-based hook into Material Design's internal password toggle (`TextInputLayout.mPasswordToggleView`). When the toggle's checked state changes, the confirm field's transformation method is synced:\n- **Checked (show):** `passwordConfirm.setTransformationMethod(null)` — displays text unmasked\n- **Unchecked (hide):** `passwordConfirm.setTransformationMethod(new PasswordTransformationMethod())` — displays text masked\n\nThe reflection is wrapped in try/catch to gracefully handle cases where the internal API might change or be unavailable.","usage":{"input_tokens":3022346,"output_tokens":44651,"cache_read_input_tokens":2661920,"total_tokens":3066997},"permission_denials":[]}
